    "result_text": "All version-2 checkpoints ran and passed. The change is complete and the full suite is green (70 tests, 0 failures/errors/skipped).\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity across the four areas the spec called out.\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation (V2 tag mixed in, region rederived inside identifiers)**\n- `MemberId.java`: added a fixed `VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` and a `regionV2(postcode, city)` that appends the tag to the plain region (`NSW` \u2192 `NSWV2`). The `memberId` now embeds `REGIONV2` instead of the plain region, so every `memberId` changes \u2014 and because the tag follows the region letters where v1 had a fiscal-year digit, no v1 `memberId` can recur. The plain `region(...)` is untouched.\n- `OwnerIdentity.java`: mixed `V2|` into the hashed inputs of both `identityKey` (still a full 64-char lowercase SHA-256 hex) and `householdId` (still deterministic per last-name+postcode), so both change while keeping their format and duplicate-detection semantics.\n- `locality`, `timezone`, and the owner segment's derived region still go through the plain `region(...)`, so the V2 tag never leaks into user-facing region fields (Cp42/Cp17/Cp30/Cp55 stay green).\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper.java`)\n- Removed top-level `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey`; added a new `OwnerIdentity` schema grouping them under a nested `identity` object, plus a top-level integer `apiVersion: 2`. The mapper builds the nested `OwnerIdentityDto` and sets `apiVersion = 2`.\n\n**Audit schema version 2** (`OwnerCreatedEvent.java` + doc in `AuditOwnerCreated.java`)\n- Added `schemaVersion` (fixed at 2) to the structured event; it now serializes `{seq, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, schemaVersion:2, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}`, carrying the v2 `memberId` (Cp53).\n\nRequest fields are unchanged; the owner-segment rule is unchanged (recomputed from the v2 identity but still keyed on the plain region, verified by Cp55).",
