    "probe_text": "I've read the full pipeline and verified each function class against the YAML. Here is the complete ordered list for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Precondition (whole endpoint)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the endpoint file requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; without it the request never enters the pipeline.\n\n## Ordered pipeline\n\nEach step below runs in this exact order. I mark whether it can **reject** (validation) or **mutate/emit** (side-effect). Every step from `checkIdentityUnique` onward runs under one shared write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`), so all the reads below see one consistent view and the whole thing commits once at the end.\n\n1. **CheckIdempotencyKey** *(validation / short-circuit)* \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key already created an owner, throws `IdempotentReplayException` \u2192 the original owner is replayed with **200** and nothing else runs. Otherwise publishes the key (possibly null) for step 15.\n\n2. **ValidateOwnerFields** *(validation + normalization side-effects)* \u2014 binds the request body once and, in this order:\n   - requires non-blank `firstName`, `lastName`;\n   - **normalizes address**: if `addressLine1` present, normalizes lines and composes `address`; else normalizes flat `address`; if neither present \u2192 `address` error;\n   - requires non-blank `city`, `telephone`;\n   - **normalizes telephone to E.164** (assumes `+61`, drops a leading `0`, strips separators; enforces 8\u201315 digits and per-country national length for `+61`/`+1`); invalid \u2192 `telephone` error;\n   - **normalizes email** (via `OwnerEmail`): syntactic check, rejects disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail.com`), lower-cases it; invalid \u2192 `email` error;\n   - validates optional `postcode` (must be 4 digits; must fall in the city's region range for Sydney/NSW, Melbourne/VIC, Brisbane/QLD);\n   - validates optional `registrationDate` (must not be in the future).\n   - Any accumulated errors \u2192 `OwnerFieldsValidationException` \u2192 **400** with an `errors` array listing each offending field. On success republishes the (mutated/normalized) DTO.\n\n3. **CheckIdentityUnique** *(validation)* \u2014 computes `identityKey = SHA-256(normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName))` and compares against every non-soft-deleted owner. A whole-key match \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409**. This is the only hard-duplicate check.\n\n4. **CheckCityCapacity** *(validation)* \u2014 counts owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n5. **BuildOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps the validated DTO onto a new `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`.\n\n6. **DefaultRegistrationDate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if no date supplied, uses server's today; then rolls weekends and listed 2026 public holidays forward to the next business day. Mutates the entity's `registrationDate` in place.\n\n7. **CheckDailyLimit** *(validation)* \u2014 counts owners already registered on that adjusted business day; if \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n8. **AssignMemberId** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `memberId = <REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (region from postcode\u2192city\u2192`UNKNOWN`, two-digit fiscal year, first 8 hex of SHA-256(telephone+lastName), Luhn check digit); on collision with an existing `memberId`, appends `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2).\n\n9. **AssignHouseholdId** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `householdId` derived from normalized lastName + postcode.\n\n10. **AssignHouseholdMemberCount** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `householdMemberCount` = existing owners sharing that `householdId` **plus one** (this new owner).\n\n11. **AssignNamesakeCount** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing firstName+lastName (case-insensitive), excluding this one.\n\n12. **AssignBulkSignupWarning** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when **more than 80** owners already exist for that business day.\n\n13. **AssignCapacityWarning** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `capacityWarning = true` when the city already holds **40\u201349** owners (approaching the cap of 50).\n\n14. **AssignPossibleDuplicate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 defaults `possibleDuplicate=false`; unless the request declared `sharesHousehold`, flags `possibleDuplicate=true` with `possibleDuplicateOf=<matching id>` when an existing non-deleted owner shares `soundex(lastName)` + postcode but has a different `identityKey`.\n\n15. **AssignMembershipLevel** *(side-effect)* \u2014 computes the points-derived level, then caps it at **one above** the max `membershipLevel` among already-persisted household members (uncapped if none); stores the capped value.\n\n16. **SaveOwner** *(side-effect \u2014 persistence)* \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)`; the id is generated here.\n\n17. **RecordIdempotencyKey** *(side-effect)* \u2014 records the `Idempotency-Key` (if any) against the new owner id in the `IdempotencyStore`, enabling future replays.\n\n18. **AuditOwnerCreated** *(side-effect \u2014 logging)* \u2014 via the `AUDIT` logger emits (a) a human-readable line (id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel) and (b) a JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent {seq, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, schemaVersion:2, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}` with a process-wide monotonic `seq`.\n\n19. **EnqueueWelcomeNotification** *(side-effect \u2014 logging)* \u2014 via the `NOTIFY` logger emits a welcome line with the owner's id and memberId.\n\n20. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** *(side-effect \u2014 response)* \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- The AGENTS.md worked example (`ValidateOwner`/`LoadOwner`/etc.) does **not** describe this endpoint \u2014 the create pipeline is far larger, and the class named `ValidateOwner` in the repo belongs to the *update* path, not create. I answered from the actual `owners.POST.yml` wiring and the function classes it references.\n- Steps 3, 4, 7, 8, 10\u201315 all count via `ownerRepository.findAll()` (full scan) inside the shared transaction; the checks and the insert therefore see one consistent snapshot.\n- Because `checkIdempotency` and `validate` run **before** the transaction-governed steps, a replayed key or a 400 avoids all the duplicate/capacity reads and the insert entirely."
